" y2="146" stroke="var(--text-muted)" stroke-width="1" vector-effect="non-scaling-stroke"></line><circle id="trdCrossD" r="2.8" fill="var(--text-primary)" stroke="var(--surface-1)" stroke-width="1.4"></circle></g></svg>
    <div class="trend-foot"><span id="toneSparkL">Fri 13:59</span><span id="toneSparkR">Thu 15:54 HKT</span></div>
    <div class="trend-read" id="toneSparkRead"></div>
    <!-- N5: the how-it-is-measured paragraph, folded. The reconciliation
         anchor above the chips STAYS visible — it prevents a real misreading
         (subtracting a chip from the headline) — while the sample counts and
         ring provenance are read once, when first curious, and never again.
         The painter keeps writing into #toneTrendNote; only where it sits
         changed. -->
    <details class="disc trend-disc"><summary><span>How this line is measured</span></summary>
    <div class="disc-body"><div class="trend-note" id="toneTrendNote">Replayed from 6,580 six-minute archive samples by this page's own scoring code, so the shape is one consistent measurement. 2,370 of them carried under 70 of 100 weight and are not plotted — a score built on a fraction of the inputs is not the same reading — which leaves 4,210 points on the line. The ring is the live headline (+20), computed from the provider's own change and range fields rather than the archive's. It sits 7 above the replay, most of it in pos.</div></div></details>
  </div>
  <div class="tone-regime" id="toneRegime"><b>No coherent regime</b><span>The 10-year, the dollar and gold are not telling one story today. The dollar is being read the textbook way and the regime itself scores neutral.</span></div>
  <div class="tone-note" id="toneNote">Most of the inputs below have aged out, so this number is being carried by the few that are left. Read it as a fragment, not as a call.</div>
  <div class="comp" id="toneComp"><div class="comp-row aged"><div class="comp-name">Macro regime<span>10y · dollar · gold, read together</span><span class="comp-age">half weight</span></div><div class="cbar"><span class="mid"></span><span class="fill" style="left:50%;width:0%;background:var(--div-pos)"></span></div><div class="comp-val">mixed</div></div><div class="comp-row"><div class="comp-name">Futures position<span>place in the session range so far</span></div><div class="cbar"><span class="mid"></span><span class="fill" style="left:39.7%;width:10.299999999999997%;background:var(--div-neg)"></span></div><div class="comp-val">40%</div></div><div class="comp-row"><div class="comp-name">Small-cap lead<span>RTY minus NQ on the day</span></div><div class="cbar"><span class="mid"></span><span class="fill" style="left:15.916666666666671%;width:34.08333333333333%;background:var(--div-neg)"></span></div><div class="comp-val">-0.82pp</div></div><div class="comp-row"><div class="comp-name">Volatility<span>VIX level and change</span></div><div class="cbar"><span class="mid"></span><span class="fill" style="left:50%;width:44.3125%;background:var(--div-pos)"></span></div><div class="comp-val">14.91</div></div><div class="comp-row"><div class="comp-name">Crude<span>distance to the long trigger</span><span class="comp-pin">pinned</span></div><div class="cbar"><span class="mid"></span><span class="fill" style="left:50%;width:50%;background:var(--div-pos)"></span></div><div class="comp-val">81.06</div></div><div class="comp-row"><div class="comp-name">Dollar<span>DXY, sign set by regime</span></div><div class="cbar"><span class="mid"></span><span class="fill" style="left:50%;width:3.45%;background:var(--div-pos)"></span></div><div class="comp-val">-0.02%</div></div><div class="comp-row"><div class="comp-name">Curve<span>2s10s slope</span></div><div class="cbar"><span class="mid"></span><span class="fill" style="left:50%;width:31.33333333333333%;background:var(--div-pos)"></span></div><div class="comp-val">+0.47</div></div></div>
  <div class="tone-break" id="toneBreak"><b>Volatility</b> is carrying the read (+15 of the +20). <b>12</b> of the 90 points of live weight sit against a rail: that share of the score cannot respond to today’s prices at all, in either direction. What would change this: enough of the components below refreshing to put more than half the weight back in play.</div>
  <div class="tone-health" id="toneHealth">Futures quotes 12m old · weights in play 90 of 100 · levels set 2026-08-03.</div>
  <button class="mini" type="button" id="toneTvBtn" style="margin-top:12px">Show table view</button>
  <div class="tvwrap" id="toneTvWrap"><table class="tvbox" id="toneTv"><tbody><tr><th>Component</th><th>Score</th><th>Weight</th><th>Value</th><th>Quote age</th></tr><tr><td>Macro regime</td><td>0</td><td>10</td><td>mixed</td><td>13.0h</td></tr><tr><td>Futures position</td><td>-21</td><td>18</td><td>40%</td><td>12m</td></tr><tr><td>Small-cap lead</td><td>-68</td><td>15</td><td>-0.82pp</td><td>12m</td></tr><tr><td>Volatility</td><td>+89</td><td>15</td><td>14.91</td><td>15s</td></tr><tr><td>Crude</td><td>+100 pinned</td><td>12</td><td>81.06</td><td>10m</td></tr><tr><td>Dollar</td><td>+7</td><td>10</td><td>-0.02%</td><td>12m</td></tr><tr><td>Curve</td><td>+63</td><td>10</td><td>+0.47</td><td>—</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
</div>

<!-- TILES -->
<div class="sectlabel" id="tilesLabel">My read — the verdict beneath each price was set at the last brief; the prices themselves refresh on their own</div>
<div class="tiles" id="tiles" data-rail="Levels" data-feeds="ES,RTY,HSI,CRUDE,VIX" data-tag="tilesLabel"><div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">ES (futures)</div><div class="tile-val">7,717.00</div><div class="tile-delta">— · an eleven-bin shelf runs 7,760.00 to 7,785.00 and it is the densest stretch on the ES map, 23.7% of the window inside eleven bins of a hundred and eighty-nine. <details class="disc tile-disc" data-tile="ES"><summary><span>The working</span></summary><div class="disc-body"> What the shelf carries has now changed four times: none at all when this tile was first written, then two straddling price, then a single one heavier than both of those together, then that same one thinning, then thickening while price walked away — then, at the payrolls print, taken whole; rebuilt within the hour as price camped on it; then taken a SECOND time by the afternoon walk to the close. 7,764.36 has since rebuilt a third time and now carries one hundred and thirteen turns, heavier than either earlier rebuild — a SIXTH state of one level: emptied, defended-and-losing, consumed, rebuilt, consumed again, rebuilt heavier. What the day left instead is the pair around it, and the reopen has been feeding the upper one all night. Well beneath, 7,755.66 no longer carries a pool at all — that structure has left the map, and the nearest survivor is four bins away and is the level this row has just described, so it is left withdrawn rather than re-pointed onto a price the paragraph already owns. OVERTAKEN — what the Asian session built here was withdrawn when it left the map, and refusing to re-point it at the cluster then sitting 1.25 bins away was right at the time. <b>7,784.24</b> is where that cluster keys now, on one hundred and four turns — and the distance between it and the price this row withdrew has been widening since the call was made. The rule the withdrawal was defending still stands — quietly moving a sentence onto a neighbouring object is how a claim stops meaning what it was written to mean. The token above hard-fails if the pool re-forms there, so this withdrawal cannot outlive its own truth. Touched within the hour. Friday’s cash session closed between the two, at 7,778.50, and Monday’s Asian hours have spent themselves building the upper edge rather than testing the lower. It sits under the cash point of control, which Wednesday moved to 7,772.50, so the price the session kept turning at and the price it spent the most time at are the same price, which is not usually true and is most of why this level is worth a tile. A pool is a different object from the bin that merely holds the most volume: it is where the session turned, not just where it sat. Here they coincide. What has changed is the side, three times in one day. The trailing session has run 7,725.50 to 7,786.75; spot spent the European morning thirty points under the shelf’s floor, the payrolls half-hour carried it back inside, the midday fade pressed the floor from beneath — and the afternoon settled it: a cash close at 7,778.50, inside the shelf, after tagging 7,786.75 through its top. The overhead resistance this tile described was real twice, and it was bought through whole twice. <b>7,820.25</b> is no longer a cluster of any kind, though it is still the top of the whole measurement: the two turns printed there have left the map — WITHDRAWN rather than re-pointed at the cluster above it, <b>7,824.50</b> on fifty-one turns, which is plainly not the two-turn object this tile described. It is why spot came off it without pausing anywhere on the way down. Below, the map is hollow down to 7,636.42; price fell into that hollow on Thursday and has climbed back out, so the hollow is underneath price again rather than around it.</div></details></div><div class="tile-bias"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--warning)"></span>Parked on a shelf</div></div><div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">RTY (futures)</div><div class="tile-val">3,007.40</div><div class="tile-delta">— · an eight-bin shelf runs 3,043.00 to 3,050.00 and spot is BENEATH it, which inverts what the shelf is for: it stops being the floor price rests on and becomes supply price has to climb back through, and 3,043.00 is that line. <details class="disc tile-disc" data-tile="RTY"><summary><span>The working</span></summary><div class="disc-body"> Overhead the shelf edge <b>3,046.45</b> is WITHDRAWN — nothing is clustered there now. It did not move: over the eleven days since this row was last measured, it and the shelves beneath it were consumed by a single object that formed across the band they occupied, <b>3,038.54</b> at eighty-six turns. The heavier structure that stood at the top of this shelf a week ago is no longer on the map at all, and price never went back to test it — it was not consumed, it dissolved as the clustering re-formed lower. What the map holds now is beneath: Monday and Tuesday between them dealt every price from 3,016.00 up to 3,045.80, which are the two sessions’ extremes and not levels. What they left is three heavyweight clusters inside the hollow this row used to call empty — 3,029.48 and 3,022.08 — carrying sixty-nine and seventy-six turns respectively — and a third that is not there any more: <b>3,036.52</b> is WITHDRAWN, with no cluster standing there now, its weight having been absorbed into 3,038.54 above. The hollow did not empty. It became the range, and the shelf above it is now the only thing on this side of the map that price has not already dealt in.</div></details></div><div class="tile-bias"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--warning)"></span>Shelf, then a hole</div></div><div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">HSI (proxy)</div><div class="tile-val">25,557.89</div><div class="tile-delta">— · prior close froze after Thursday and thawed to the wrong number — it is still wrong on the new vendor, so the fault was never the vendor</div><div class="tile-bias"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--critical)"></span>Level only</div></div><div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">WTI crude</div><div class="tile-val">81.06</div><div class="tile-delta">— · the only reference still frozen — read the level: 81.51 and 81 both went on Sunday's reopen in one six-minute gap, not on Friday; 80 has traded both sides since</div><div class="tile-bias"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--critical)"></span>Trigger fired</div></div><div class="tile"><div class="tile-label">VIX (cash)</div><div class="tile-val">14.91</div><div class="tile-delta">— · cash, and the percentage is suppressed — the reference this tile measured from was wrong in sign, printing a fall on a day vol rose; the level is sound, the change is not</div><div class="tile-bias"><span class="dot" style="background:var(--critical)"></span>Level only</div></div></div>

<!-- SESSION CLOCK -->
<section class="card" id="rail-session-clock">
  <div class="card-head">
    <div class="card-title">Session clock</div>
    <div class="card-sub"><details class="fwork fwork-sub"><summary>The same level break means different things at different hours. </summary><div class="fwork-b">This is where the clock is now, in Hong Kong time, and how much a break is worth here. Bar height is how far a break tends to follow through — it is a judgement from how these hours normally behave, not a measured statistic. Grey means the contract is shut.</div></details></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <div class="sess-now" id="sessNow"><div class="sess-lab">Right now · Hong Kong time</div><div class="sess-name">Europe opens · HK closes</div><div class="sess-meta">15:00–16:10 HKT · it is 15:57</div><div class="sess-trust"><u><i class="on" style="height:4px"></i><i class="on" style="height:8px"></i><i class="" style="height:12px"></i></u>Break follow-through: Moderate</div><div class="sess-mhi"><span class="mchip on">MHI OPEN</span><span>HK afternoon — it runs 20 min past the cash close · <b>33m</b> to the change</span></div><div class="sess-note">Europe arrives and RTY and ES get their first genuine two-way flow of the day. This is the earliest hour a US level break is worth trusting. The cash index closes at 16:10 into it; MHI keeps trading until 16:30, so the last twenty minutes of the HK day are the contract moving with no index behind it.</div><div class="sess-meta" style="margin-top:9px">Frozen at the snapshot time above. Open this in Safari or Chrome and the clock tracks live.</div></div>
    <div class="sess-strip" id="sessStrip"><div class="sess-axis"></div><div class="sess-seg" id="sseg0" style="left: 0%; width: calc(4.16667% - 2px); height: 11px;"></div><div class="sess-seg" id="sseg1" style="left: 4.16667%; width: calc(8.33333% - 2px); height: 30px;"></div><div class="sess-seg" id="sseg2" style="left: 12.5%; width: calc(4.16667% - 2px); height: 30px;"></div><div class="sess-seg" id="sseg3" style="left: 16.6667%; width: calc(4.16667% - 2px); height: 11px;"></div><div class="sess-seg shut" id="sseg4" style="left: 20.8333%; width: calc(4.16667% - 2px); height: 5px;"></div><div class="sess-seg" id="sseg5" style="left: 25%; width: calc(12.5% - 2px); height: 11px;"></div><div class="sess-seg" id="sseg6" style="left: 37.5%; width: calc(2.08333% - 2px); height: 11px;"></div><div class="sess-seg" id="sseg7" style="left: 39.5833%; width: calc(10.4167% - 2px); height: 20px;"></div><div class="sess-seg" id="sseg8" style="left: 50%; width: calc(4.16667% - 2px); height: 11px;"></div><div class="sess-seg" id="sseg9" style="left: 54.1667%; width: calc(8.33333% - 2px); height: 20px;"></div><div class="sess-seg cur" id="sseg10" style="left: 62.5%; width: calc(4.86111% - 2px); height: 20px;"></div><div class="sess-seg" id="sseg11" style="left: 67.3611%; width: calc(18.0556% - 2px); height: 20px;"></div><div class="sess-seg" id="sseg12" style="left: 85.4167%; width: calc(4.16667% - 2px); height: 11px;"></div><div class="sess-seg" id="sseg13" style="left: 89.5833%; width: calc(4.16667% - 2px); height: 30px;"></div><div class="sess-seg" id="sseg14" style="left: 93.75%; width: calc(6.25% - 2px); height: 11px;"></div><div class="sess-tick" style="left: 0px; transform: none;">00:00</div><div class="sess-tick" style="left: 25%;">06:00</div><div class="sess-tick" style="left: 50%;">12:00</div><div class="sess-tick" style="left: 75%;">18:00</div><div class="sess-tick" style="left: auto; right: 0px; transform: none;">24:00</div><div class="sess-now-mk" id="sessMk" style="left: 66.4583%;"></div></div>
    <div class="sess-key">Taller bar = a break here is more likely to keep going · the vertical line is now · the outlined bar is the phase you are in</div>
    <div class="sess-next" id="sessNext">In <b>13m</b> this becomes <b>European session</b> · 16:10 HKT <span style="color:var(--text-muted)">(moderate follow-through)</span></div>
    <button class="mini" type="button" id="sessTvBtn" style="margin-top:12px">Show table view</button>
    <div class="tvwrap" id="sessTvWrap"><table class="tvbox" id="sessTv"><thead><tr><th>Window (HKT)</th><th>Phase</th><th>Follow-through</th></tr></thead><tbody><tr><td>00:00–01:00</td><td style="text-align:left;white-space:normal">US midday lull</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>01:00–03:00</td><td style="text-align:left;white-space:normal">US afternoon trend</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>03:00–04:00</td><td style="text-align:left;white-space:normal">Power hour → cash close</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>04:00–05:00</td><td style="text-align:left;white-space:normal">After the US cash close</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>05:00–06:00</td><td style="text-align:left;white-space:normal">CME halt — futures shut</td><td>Shut</td></tr><tr><td>06:00–09:00</td><td style="text-align:left;white-space:normal">Globex reopen · Asia pre-dawn</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>09:00–09:30</td><td style="text-align:left;white-space:normal">HK pre-open auction</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>09:30–12:00</td><td style="text-align:left;white-space:normal">HK morning session</td><td>Moderate</td></tr><tr><td>12:00–13:00</td><td style="text-align:left;white-space:normal">HK lunch break</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>13:00–15:00</td><td style="text-align:left;white-space:normal">HK afternoon session</td><td>Moderate</td></tr><tr><td>15:00–16:10</td><td style="text-align:left;white-space:normal">Europe opens · HK closes</td><td>Moderate</td></tr><tr><td>16:10–20:30</td><td style="text-align:left;white-space:normal">European session</td><td>Moderate</td></tr><tr><td>20:30–21:30</td><td style="text-align:left;white-space:normal">US data window · pre-open</td><td>Low</td></tr><tr><td>21:30–22:30</td><td style="text-align:left;white-space:normal">US cash open — first hour</td><td>High</td></tr><tr><td>22:30–24:00</td><td style="text-align:left;white-space:normal">US midday lull</td><td>Low</td></tr></tbody></table></div>
  </div>
</section>

<!-- DAY SHAPE -->
<!-- data-feeds is ES,RTY and that is the whole list on purpose. The card is a
     measurement over the bar archive, and the relay banks bars for these two
     contracts only; NQ, YM and HSI arrive as a six-minute quote sample, which is
     coarser than the half-hour bucket this card counts in and would report the
     sampler's step size as the market's movement. The one live number here is
     the open contract's range so far, read to divide by the cumulative curve. -->
<section class="card" data-feeds="ES,RTY" id="rail-day-shape">
  <div class="card-title-anchor" id="seasCard"></div>
  <div class="card-head">
    <div class="card-title">Day shape — when the movement actually happens</div>
    <div class="card-sub"><details class="fwork fwork-sub"><summary>Seasonality of the <b>clock</b>, not the calendar. </summary><div class="fwork-b">Two things are counted per half hour and never merged: <b>travel</b>, the sum of the bars’ own high-lows, which adds up to the whole day and answers <i>when did the tape move</i>; and <b>range</b>, high minus low, which does not add up and answers <i>how far did price actually get</i>. Their ratio says how much of a session’s motion turns into displacement. The third panel is the part you can act on — how much of a typical day’s range is already behind you by now. No day-of-week table and no direction rate are emitted; the disclosure says why, and gives the date the first of them becomes measurable.</div></details></div>
  </div>
  <div class="ctl-row">
    <div class="tabs" id="seasTabs" role="tablist"><button class="tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="true">ES</button><button class="tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false">NQ</button><button class="tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false">RTY</button><button class="tab" type="button" role="tab" aria-selected="false">YM</button></div>
  </div>
  <div class="card-body">
    <!-- Which contracts have no tab above, and why. Under the tabs because that
         is where a reader notices the absence: the four tabs are the answer to
         "which contracts does this card cover", and a fifth on the relay with no
         tab is a question the card should answer rather than leave. Empty and
         invisible when every contract is covered. -->
    <div class="seas-absent" id="seasAbsent"><div class="sab-row sab-never"><b>HSI is not coming, and that is not about the size of the archive.</b> A day counts on this card only when its bars span every one of the 3 killzones, because every figure here is a share of one whole day’s travel and a partial day has no denominator. HSI is the Hong Kong cash index, whose day sits inside Asia and London: across 1,089 bars and 16 day-labels its best day has reached 2 of the 3 and has never reached more, and its widest single day spans 6.6 hours of the twenty-four a killzone day covers. No amount of waiting closes that gap, so “coming” would be false. What CAN be measured on those hours is measured — the Hong Kong structure has its own board on the tape card, built on the future that actually trades.</div></div>
    <div class="seas-now" id="seasNow">It is <b>15:57 HKT</b> (07:57Z), the <b>London</b> session — half hour <b>24 of 48</b> since the last cash close. On a typical day ES has made <b>38%</b> of its range by this point (21 days) and has <b>67%</b> of its movement still ahead.</div>
    <div class="seas-plot" id="seasPlot"><div class="seas-pan"><div class="seas-pan-h"><span><b>Travel</b> — share of the day’s movement</span><span>one bar = 30 min</span></div><div class="seas-frame" style="height: 80px;"><div class="seas-band" style="left: calc(0%); width: calc(4.16667%);"></div><div class="seas-band b2" style="left: calc(8.33333%); width: calc(37.5%);"></div><div class="seas-zlab" style="left: calc(8.33333%); background: var(--surface-1);">Asia</div><div class="seas-band" style="left: calc(45.8333%); width: calc(27.0833%);"></div><div class="seas-zlab" style="left: calc(45.8333%); background: var(--plane);">London</div><div class="seas-band b2" style="left: calc(72.9167%); width: calc(27.0833%);"></div><div class="seas-zlab" style="left: calc(72.9167%); background: var(--surface-1);">New York</div><div class="seas-gl" style="bottom: 40px;"></div><div class="seas-glab" style="bottom: 40px;">6.3%</div><div class="seas-gl" style="bottom: 80px;"></div><div class="seas-glab" style="bottom: 80px;">12.5%</div><div class="seas-bar dim" title="04:00 HKT · travel 2.51% of the day, 16 days" style="left: calc(0% + 1px); width: calc(2.08333% - 2px); height: 16.0832px;"></div><div class="seas-bar dim" title="04:30 HKT · travel 1.22% of the day, 16 days" style="left: calc(2.08333% + 1px); width: calc(2.08333% - 2px); height: 7.7888px;"></div><div class="seas-bar dim" title="06:00 HKT · travel 1.82% of the day, 20 days" style="left: calc(8.33333% + 1px); width: calc(2.08333% - 2px); height: 11.6352px;"></div><div class="seas-bar dim" title="06:30 HKT · travel 1.10% of the day, 20 days" style="left: calc(10.4167% + 1px); width: calc(2.08333% - 2px); height: 7.072px;"></div><div class="seas-bar dim" title="07:00 HKT · travel 1.00% of the day, 20 days" style="left: calc(12.5% + 1px); width: calc(2.08333% - 2px); height: 6.4128px;"></div><div class="seas-bar dim" title="07:30 HKT · travel 1.47% of the day, 20 days" style="left: calc(14.5833% + 1px); width: calc(2.0