    <div class="curve-stat" id="curveStat"><div>2s10s<b>+0.47</b></div><div>2y<b>4.19</b></div><div>10y<b>4.66</b></div><div>30y<b>5.18</b></div></div>
    <div class="yc-chg" id="curveChg"><div>1M<b>▲ +1.0</b><u>bp</u></div><div>3M<b>▼ -1.0</b><u>bp</u></div><div>6M<b>▼ -1.0</b><u>bp</u></div><div>1Y<b>▲ +1.0</b><u>bp</u></div><div>2Y<b>▲ +2.0</b><u>bp</u></div><div>5Y<b>▲ +2.0</b><u>bp</u></div><div>10Y<b>▲ +2.0</b><u>bp</u></div><div>30Y<b>▲ +1.0</b><u>bp</u></div></div>
    <div class="yc-move" id="curveMove"><strong>level held, shape held</strong><em>level +0.9bp · 2s10s 0.0bp · Tue, 25 Aug → Wed, 26 Aug</em></div>
    <div class="advis" id="curveAdv"><span class="advis-hdr">What this move implies</span>Neither the level nor the shape moved by as much as a basis point at any tenor. <b>This is a publication, not a move</b>, and nothing on the rest of this page should be re-read because of it. Level moved <b>+0.9bp</b> on average and 2s10s by <b>0.0bp</b>, with the belly underperforming both ends by 2.0bp. Over the whole 21-curve window the net is <b>level held, steeper</b> (level -0.3bp, 2s10s +2.0bp), so a single day against that direction is noise until it is two. <div class="subnote">The paragraph above is a <b>framework, not a measurement</b>. It is the standard reading of the shape, applied to numbers this page did compute; it is not what this archive has been observed to do, because this archive holds 20 moves. What was actually observed is in the disclosure below, as rows rather than as a rate.</div></div>
    <details class="disc">
      <summary><span id="curveSum"><span>This history is <b>21 curves and 20 moves</b>, not the 6,573 rows it was read from — too short to carry a hit rate, and it does not carry one. Open for all 20, what ES did after each, and how the shape is decomposed.</span></span></summary>
      <div class="disc-body" id="curveBody"><p><b>The sample is 21, not 6,573.</b> The relay archive holds 6,573 rows carrying a yield object, and that number is a trap. Treasury publishes constant-maturity yields <b>once per business day</b>, around 19:50 UTC, and the relay resamples every few minutes — so those rows contain 21 distinct curves, each repeated a few hundred times. Averaging over rows would weight a curve by how long the relay happened to be running while it was current, which is a fact about the relay and not about the market. Everything on this card is computed on the 21 curves and the 20 transitions between them.</p><table class="disc-tbl"><tbody><tr><th>Published</th><th>2y</th><th>10y</th><th>30y</th><th>2s10s</th><th>Samples</th></tr><tr><td>Thu, 30 Jul <span style="color:var(--text-muted)">first</span></td><td>4.22</td><td>4.67</td><td>5.20</td><td>+0.45</td><td>80</td></tr><tr><td>Fri, 31 Jul 05:59 <span class="yc-odd">off-cycle</span></td><td>4.23</td><td>4.68</td><td>5.21</td><td>+0.45</td><td>138</td></tr><tr><td>Fri, 31 Jul 19:48</td><td>4.28</td><td>4.75</td><td>5.27</td><td>+0.47</td><td>721</td></tr><tr><td>Mon, 3 Aug</td><td>4.25</td><td>4.70</td><td>5.23</td><td>+0.45</td><td>239</td></tr><tr><td>Tue, 4 Aug</td><td>4.20</td><td>4.63</td><td>5.18</td><td>+0.43</td><td>240</td></tr><tr><td>Wed, 5 Aug</td><td>4.18</td><td>4.63</td><td>5.17</td><td>+0.45</td><td>240</td></tr><tr><td>Thu, 6 Aug</td><td>4.25</td><td>4.69</td><td>5.22</td><td>+0.44</td><td>242</td></tr><tr><td>Fri, 7 Aug</td><td>4.19</td><td>4.65</td><td>5.19</td><td>+0.46</td><td>718</td></tr><tr><td>Mon, 10 Aug</td><td>4.25</td><td>4.72</td><td>5.25</td><td>+0.47</td><td>240</td></tr><tr><td>Tue, 11 Aug</td><td>4.22</td><td>4.70</td><td>5.24</td><td>+0.48</td><td>243</td></tr><tr><td>Wed, 12 Aug</td><td>4.20</td><td>4.68</td><td>5.24</td><td>+0.48</td><td>242</td></tr><tr><td>Thu, 13 Aug</td><td>4.15</td><td>4.63</td><td>5.21</td><td>+0.48</td><td>232</td></tr><tr><td>Fri, 14 Aug</td><td>4.17</td><td>4.68</td><td>5.25</td><td>+0.51</td><td>721</td></tr><tr><td>Mon, 17 Aug</td><td>4.19</td><td>4.72</td><td>5.31</td><td>+0.53</td><td>338</td></tr><tr><td>Wed, 19 Aug <span class="yc-odd">off-cycle</span></td><td>4.19</td><td>4.71</td><td>5.28</td><td>+0.52</td><td>189</td></tr><tr><td>Thu, 20 Aug 01:00 <span class="yc-odd">off-cycle</span></td><td>4.19</td><td>4.65</td><td>5.19</td><td>+0.46</td><td>188</td></tr><tr><td>Thu, 20 Aug 19:48</td><td>4.19</td><td>4.69</td><td>5.23</td><td>+0.50</td><td>242</td></tr><tr><td>Fri, 21 Aug</td><td>4.24</td><td>4.74</td><td>5.27</td><td>+0.50</td><td>719</td></tr><tr><td>Mon, 24 Aug</td><td>4.24</td><td>4.70</td><td>5.23</td><td>+0.46</td><td>239</td></tr><tr><td>Tue, 25 Aug</td><td>4.17</td><td>4.64</td><td>5.17</td><td>+0.47</td><td>241</td></tr><tr><td>Wed, 26 Aug</td><td>4.19</td><td>4.66</td><td>5.18</td><td>+0.47</td><td>121</td></tr></tbody></table><p>A curve marked <b>off-cycle</b> first appeared outside the publication window — a late fill, a revision, or the relay reconnecting mid-session. The first row is marked <b>first</b> rather than off-cycle, because it is whatever was current when the archive began and calling it odd would blame the data for having a beginning.</p><p><b>What ES did next, as rows.</b> For each transition, ES from the moment the curve changed to the same clock time one trading session later. Not a rate — 20 events cannot support one, and a percentage computed on 20 reads exactly like a percentage computed on four hundred.</p><table class="disc-tbl"><tbody><tr><th>Date</th><th>What the curve did</th><th>Level</th><th>2s10s</th><th>ES next session</th></tr><tr><td>Fri, 31 Jul 05:59</td><td>yields up, shape held</td><td>+1.2</td><td>0.0</td><td><b style="color:var(--up)">+0.76%</b> <span style="color:var(--text-muted)">over the weekend</span></td></tr><tr><td>Fri, 31 Jul 19:48</td><td>yields up, steeper</td><td>+3.6</td><td>+2.0</td><td><b style="color:var(--up)">+1.21%</b> <span style="color:var(--text-muted)">over the weekend</span></td></tr><tr><td>Mon, 3 Aug</td><td>level held, flatter</td><td>-0.6</td><td>-2.0</td><td><b style="color:var(--up)">+1.79%</b></td></tr><tr><td>Tue, 4 Aug</td><td>yields down, flatter</td><td>-4.0</td><td>-2.0</td><td><b style="color:var(--down)">-0.04%</b></td></